{"rulings":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-17e84003","decision":"reject","rationale":"In the actual review worktree (`.claude/worktrees/tanksim-6e5.4.7`), `molt_cycle` still uses one shared timer and fixed accumulator adjustments: success applies `-0.35` and failure applies `+0.3` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:398-403`. There are no `failed_stage_count` or `successful_stage_count` variables in this branch. The amendment’s premise comes from a different code version, so it does not identify a real issue in the code under review."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-2df09666","decision":"reject","rationale":"`update_molt_stress` does contain an unguarded `/ params.gh_min_d` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:336-338`, and invariants allow `gh_min_d == 0.0` via `check_non_negative` at `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs:291-298`. But `gh_d()` is clamped non-negative in `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs:203-210`, so when `gh_min_d == 0.0` the branch condition `gh_d < params.gh_min_d` cannot be satisfied. That leaves no reachable divide-by-zero defect. The amendment’s additional consistency argument also depends on `molt_mineral_modifier`, which is not present in this review branch. On balance this is a defensive cleanup suggestion, not a required amendment."}],"summary":"Both disputed amendments are rejected. In the review worktree, `fr-3-17e84003` is based on code that is not present, and `fr-3-2df09666` points to an unreachable defensive edge case rather than a concrete correctness defect."}